dsided us quite so hard as the  first The Hitcher a young man picks up a  hitchhiker by the side of the highway in  the middle of nowhere on a dark and  stormy night that's a pretty spooky  premise on its own but 1986 is The  Hitcher quickly turns it into something  even more sinister with an opening scene  to left audiences with no doubts about  where the movie was going this opening  scene introduces Rutger Hauer Jean  Reiter as an agent of pure mayhem and  how his performance makes his previous  turn as psychotic replicant Roy batty  and Blade Runner looked positively  endearing by comparison of all dead  horror film fans had plenty of reason to  be wary of 2013 soft reboot of Sam  Raimi's classic Evil Dead but those fans  had no way of knowing at the time that  the project was in the hands of a major  Talent writer / director fede alvarez  who made no attempt to rehash what had  worked in the previous series but  brought a wickedly inventive tone all  his own instead the film opens with a  terrified young woman being hunted down  and captured in the woods by her own  family who appear to be religious  fanatics bent on burning her alive but  as her father fumbles with the matches  the woman's tearful please take a hard  left turn and it suddenly becomes  obvious that the only terrible mistake  this family made was not getting that  fire started a lot sooner thanks for  watching click the looper icon to  subscribe to our YouTube channel plus  check out all this cool stuff we know  you'll love to  [Music]
 

